{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Structured Outputs & Constrained Decoding Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: regex-constrained generation from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py` for a standalone FSM implementation. The core idea in 30 lines:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mask_logits(logits, valid_token_ids):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask = [float(\"-inf\")] * len(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for tid in valid_token_ids:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mask[tid] = logits[tid]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mask"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def generate_constrained(model, tokenizer, prompt, fsm):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ids = tokenizer.encode(prompt)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    state = fsm.initial_state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while not fsm.is_accept(state):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = model.next_token_logits(ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        valid = fsm.valid_tokens(state, tokenizer)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = mask_logits(logits, valid)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tok = sample(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ids.append(tok)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        state = fsm.transition(state, tok)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokenizer.decode(ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The FSM tracks what parts of the grammar we have satisfied so far. `valid_tokens(state, tokenizer)` computes which vocabulary tokens can advance the FSM without leaving an accepting path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Outlines for JSON Schema"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from pydantic import BaseModel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from typing import Literal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import outlines"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Review(BaseModel):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sentiment: Literal[\"positive\", \"negative\", \"neutral\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    confidence: float"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    evidence_span: str"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = outlines.models.transformers(\"meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "generator = outlines.generate.json(model, Review)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = generator(\"Classify: 'The wait staff was attentive and the food arrived hot.'\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(result)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Review(sentiment='positive', confidence=0.93, evidence_span='attentive ... hot')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Zero validation errors. Ever. The FSM makes invalid output unreachable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Instructor for provider-agnostic Pydantic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import instructor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from anthropic import Anthropic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from pydantic import BaseModel, Field"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Invoice(BaseModel):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vendor: str"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_usd: float = Field(ge=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    line_items: list[str]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "client = instructor.from_anthropic(Anthropic())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "invoice = client.messages.create("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model=\"claude-opus-4-7\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_tokens=1024,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response_model=Invoice,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Extract from: 'Acme Corp $420. Widget, Gizmo.'\"}],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Different mechanism. Instructor does not touch logits. It formats the schema into the prompt, parses the output, and retries on validation failure (default 3 times). Works with any provider. Retries add latency and cost. Cross-provider portability is the selling point."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: native vendor APIs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from openai import OpenAI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "client = OpenAI()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "response = client.responses.create("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model=\"gpt-5\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    input=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Classify: 'The food was cold.'\"}],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    text={\"format\": {\"type\": \"json_schema\", \"name\": \"sentiment\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          \"schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"required\": [\"sentiment\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                     \"properties\": {\"sentiment\": {\"type\": \"string\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                                                  \"enum\": [\"positive\", \"negative\", \"neutral\"]}}}}},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(response.output_parsed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Server-side constrained decoding. Reliability parity with Outlines for supported schemas. No local model management. Locks you to the vendor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Prompt a small open-weights model (e.g., Llama-3.2-3B) without constrained decoding for `Review(sentiment, confidence, evidence_span)`. Measure the fraction that parse as valid JSON on 100 reviews.\n2. **Medium.** Same corpus with Outlines JSON mode. Compare compliance rate, latency, and semantic accuracy.\n3. **Hard.** Implement a regex-constrained decoder from scratch for phone numbers (`\\d{3}-\\d{3}-\\d{4}`). Verify 0 invalid outputs on 1000 samples."
      ]
    }
